WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.766 --> 00:00:05.238
♪ ♪

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:07.273 align:start size:91% position:9%
ERIN: We love working
with all kinds of animals,

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.642 align:start size:91% position:9%
but every once in a while,
something comes along

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:12.645 align:start size:81% position:19%
that gets everybody
really excited.

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:14.447 line:0%
We got llamas coming today.

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:18.584 align:start size:78% position:22% line:0%
Like, this is like
a jackpot day.

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:19.919
Hey, how are you?

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:21.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
BRIAN: Doing good. Hi, Ben.
ERIN: Good to see you.

00:00:21.153 --> 00:00:23.089
BEN: Hey, how are you?
BRIAN: I'm doing great.

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:25.124 align:start size:81% position:19%
BEN: Llamas are rare
in Nebraska,

00:00:25.124 --> 00:00:28.294 align:start size:97% position:3%
and today we have three llamas
coming in all at once.

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:29.328
ERIN: So, this is your herd?

00:00:29.328 --> 00:00:30.430
BRIAN: So far.
LORI: So far.

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:31.797
ERIN: So far.

00:00:31.797 --> 00:00:34.600 line:0%
LORI: Brian's wife and I
have been lifelong friends,

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.637 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
and while at the Nebraska
State Fair last year

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:40.172 align:start position:0%
we decided, "Hey, let's kind of
have a mid-life crisis

00:00:40.172 --> 00:00:42.008
and buy some llamas."

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:44.143
ERIN: I can't wait
to meet your babies.

00:00:44.143 --> 00:00:46.446 align:start position:0%
BRIAN: I went to the state fair
and there are these llamas,

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:49.181
and they drew me in
and hypnotized me,

00:00:49.181 --> 00:00:50.316
and I knew that was it.

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:51.951
I just had to have a llama.

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:53.119
That's Temptress.

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:54.487
ERIN: Hi, pretty girl.

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:56.155 align:start position:0%
BEN: We used to call you
temptress in college, didn't we?

00:00:56.155 --> 00:00:58.691
ERIN: Oh, shut up.
You did not. That's--

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:01.427
LORI: There's Golden Boy.

00:01:01.427 --> 00:01:03.062
ERIN: Hi.

00:01:03.062 --> 00:01:04.330
BRIAN: And that's Thunder.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.365
BEN: You are cool.

00:01:06.365 --> 00:01:09.402 align:start size:97% position:3%
ERIN: So our lovely lady llama
was bred earlier this year,

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:12.038 align:start size:91% position:9%
and she's here today
to see if she's pregnant.

00:01:12.038 --> 00:01:14.073
The llamas on parade.

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:17.710
But first, a round of vaccines
and dewormer for the whole crew.

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:18.711
BEN: Okay, guys, ready?

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:20.513
I'm going to pinch a little bit.

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:21.714
BRIAN: Good boy.
BEN: Okay, good.

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:22.881
BRIAN: Alright.

00:01:22.881 --> 00:01:24.784
BEN: Alright, now, we'll
give him his dewormer.

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:26.585
I'm glad he threw
all three llamas in

00:01:26.585 --> 00:01:28.554
because they're pack animals,

00:01:28.554 --> 00:01:30.423 align:start size:84% position:16%
they like the comfort
of each other.

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:31.424
Good, alright.

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:33.393
One down.

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:34.893 align:start size:88% position:13%
BRIAN: Okay, ready boy?
BEN: Ready, guys?

00:01:34.893 --> 00:01:36.462
BRIAN: Hold on, boy, hold on.

00:01:36.462 --> 00:01:39.933 align:start size:88% position:13%
ERIN: Llamas are kind of
wiggly to hang on to.

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:41.401
BRIAN: Hold on.

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:42.468
Didn't like that, did you?

00:01:42.468 --> 00:01:44.370
Nope.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.606
And she by far is the most
sensitive to being handled.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:47.973
BEN: Oh, great.

00:01:47.973 --> 00:01:50.209
ERIN: Do you want to just
try her in the stall, Ben?

00:01:50.209 --> 00:01:53.312 align:start size:91% position:9%
BEN: Yeah. She has
more manpower than we do.

00:01:53.312 --> 00:01:55.214 align:start size:91% position:9%
So, we're going to put her
in a safe place

00:01:55.214 --> 00:01:56.616
and get her done safely.

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:59.385
ERIN: She's going
to the padded room.

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:00.687 align:start size:78% position:22%
BRIAN: Easy, girl.
BEN: I'm in.

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:01.687
ERIN: Good girl.

00:02:01.687 --> 00:02:02.722
BRIAN: Easy, girl.

00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:04.623
Whoa, baby, good girl.

00:02:04.623 --> 00:02:05.725
BEN: Hold it.
BRIAN: Hold on.

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:09.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
BEN: Good.
BRIAN: Ah, the rodeo. Whoa.

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:10.396 align:start size:81% position:19%
BEN: Got those
big, old long necks.

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:12.231 align:start size:88% position:13%
ERIN: Their necks,
it's like waa, waa, waa!

00:02:12.231 --> 00:02:13.466
I think I wanna get ya.

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:14.500
Then I'm gonna spit on ya.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:16.001
Then when you're not looking

00:02:16.001 --> 00:02:17.870 align:start size:97% position:3%
and you're moving away from my
spit, I'm going to kick ya.

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:19.639 align:start size:97% position:3%
BRIAN: Yeah, they're
very powerful for their size,

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:20.907
that's for sure.

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:22.808
BEN: She could bite.

00:02:22.808 --> 00:02:24.077
BRIAN: Easy, girl.

00:02:24.077 --> 00:02:25.077
Did you get her?

00:02:25.077 --> 00:02:26.512
(gurgles)

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:28.181
Oh, boy, that don't sound good.

00:02:28.181 --> 00:02:29.182
ERIN: Oh!

00:02:29.182 --> 00:02:30.183
BRIAN: There you go.

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:31.350 align:start size:81% position:19%
ERIN: Are you okay?
MONTE: Yeah.

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:33.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
BEN: We're going to give her
a little more.

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:35.388
She spit half of it out.

00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:37.189
(laughter)

00:02:37.189 --> 00:02:39.224
BRIAN: So, you had your
worming for the year.

00:02:39.224 --> 00:02:42.195 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
ERIN: Temptress is being
a typical llama.

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:45.097 align:start position:0% line:0%
BEN: I've done a lot of horses,
they never do that.

00:02:45.097 --> 00:02:46.432
(laughing)

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:48.200 align:start size:91% position:9%
ERIN: A llama's
natural defense mechanism

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:50.269 align:start size:84% position:16%
is to actually take
their stomach contents

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:52.705
and regurgitate it right at you.

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:55.674 align:start size:91% position:9%
BEN: A llama's spit
can travel up to 15 feet.

00:02:55.674 --> 00:02:58.077 align:start size:78% position:22%
ERIN: There!
BRIAN: Good girl.

00:02:58.077 --> 00:03:00.546
BEN: Now, we get to see
if she's gonna be a mama.

00:03:00.546 --> 00:03:02.114
We're going to have to
put on the ultrasound

00:03:02.114 --> 00:03:03.582
and get a picture here.

00:03:03.582 --> 00:03:05.785 align:start size:97% position:3%
This is the screen that you're
going to be able to watch.

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:07.019
And you can just hold this.

00:03:07.019 --> 00:03:08.020 align:start size:84% position:16%
You'll see everything
I'm seeing.

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:08.955
MONTE: Okay.
BEN: Alright?

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:10.089
MONTE: Alright.

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:11.791 align:start size:94% position:6%
BEN: And the most definitive
thing to see

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:13.626 align:start size:88% position:13%
would be really any part
of the baby,

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:15.795 align:start size:78% position:22%
but a heartbeat
would be the best,

00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:18.797 align:start size:97% position:3%
because then we know
the baby's viable, it's alive,

00:03:18.797 --> 00:03:22.534 align:start size:97% position:3%
and everything is going to be
A-OK hopefully.

00:03:22.534 --> 00:03:25.104 align:start size:84% position:16%
BRIAN: We're hoping
for a positive result.

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:26.105
BEN: It's okay.

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:28.307
Got to move slow.

00:03:28.307 --> 00:03:30.309
She's doing so good.

00:03:30.309 --> 00:03:33.446 align:start size:88% position:13%
I'm not seeing
anything obvious, guys.

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:35.147
That's not a good sign.

00:03:35.147 --> 00:03:39.385
Really, all I see is food
material at this point.

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:42.054 align:start size:91% position:9%
We could draw blood on her
if we're inconclusive,

00:03:42.054 --> 00:03:44.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it's more gratifying
just to ultrasound her belly

00:03:44.356 --> 00:03:45.525
and see if we can see that baby.

00:03:45.525 --> 00:03:46.992
One more try.

00:03:46.992 --> 00:03:49.795 align:start position:0%
We're going to keep looking,
because I don't like to give up.

00:03:49.795 --> 00:03:52.465 align:start size:88% position:13%
ERIN: In llamas there's
less amniotic fluid

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:54.800 align:start size:84% position:16%
proportionately
surrounding that cria,

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:56.468
which is a baby llama.

00:03:56.468 --> 00:03:59.639 align:start position:0%
It's not just like a lady that's
like, "Yep, it's right here."

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:01.707 align:start size:91% position:9%
You kind of got to go
on a little bit of a hunt

00:04:01.707 --> 00:04:04.143 align:start size:88% position:13%
to figure out where
she's tucking this baby

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:07.413
if there is one there.

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:09.281 align:start size:78% position:22%
BEN: I think I see
something now.

00:04:09.281 --> 00:04:11.083
When I get further down.

00:04:11.083 --> 00:04:12.451
ERIN: That looks
like a heartbeat.

00:04:12.451 --> 00:04:13.719
BEN: I know!

00:04:13.719 --> 00:04:14.721 align:start size:91% position:9%
MONTE: Right there,
that's going right there?

00:04:14.721 --> 00:04:15.788
ERIN: Yeah, mm-hmm.

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:17.089 align:start size:84% position:16%
BEN: Hundred percent,
she's pregnant.

00:04:17.089 --> 00:04:18.090
That looks like a cria!

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:20.159 align:start size:91% position:9%
ERIN: She's a llama mama.
Woo-hoo!

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:21.327
BRIAN: Alright, yay!

00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:22.395
BEN: Good.

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:24.496 align:start size:78% position:22%
ERIN: You guys
are having a baby.

00:04:24.496 --> 00:04:25.597
BEN: So exciting.

00:04:25.597 --> 00:04:27.266
She's about nine months along,

00:04:27.266 --> 00:04:29.668
and their gestation is
11 months to 12 months,

00:04:29.668 --> 00:04:31.103
and I've heard even 13 months.

00:04:31.103 --> 00:04:32.471
So, that's kind of crazy

00:04:32.471 --> 00:04:34.940 align:start position:0%
that they can hold these babies
inside them over a year.

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:37.176 align:start position:0%
BRIAN: This is the most
wonderful thing to happen to us.

00:04:37.176 --> 00:04:38.844 align:start size:84% position:16%
Now we know that we're
gonna have a baby

00:04:38.844 --> 00:04:40.078
coming in a few months,

00:04:40.078 --> 00:04:41.514
and then we can start thinking

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:43.449 align:start size:88% position:13%
about building
a larger herd from that.

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:44.850
Good girl, mama.

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:47.786
You are an official mama llama.

00:04:47.786 --> 00:04:53.659
♪ ♪

00:04:53.659 --> 00:04:55.828
ERIN: It decided to rain today.

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:58.097
We're at an unusual
house call today.

00:04:58.097 --> 00:04:59.165
Hey, it's good to see you.

00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:00.499
MARY: Good to see you!

00:05:00.499 --> 00:05:02.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
ERIN: Our good client, Mary,
has some concerns

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:04.903 align:start size:88% position:13%
about a neighborhood cat
she cares for.

00:05:04.903 --> 00:05:07.507
She can't get near this cat
to get it to the clinic.

00:05:07.507 --> 00:05:10.576 align:start size:88% position:13%
So, she needs our expert
cat-catching help.

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:11.911
MARY: It's one heck
of a house call.

00:05:11.911 --> 00:05:13.278
ERIN: Oh, you betcha.

00:05:13.278 --> 00:05:16.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, I feel like I brought
like my team of ninjas.

00:05:16.248 --> 00:05:17.850 line:0%
MARY: We appreciate how well

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:20.886 line:0%
Dr. Ben and Erin
take care of cats.

00:05:20.886 --> 00:05:23.956 line:0%
Cats of course are the most
important patients they see.

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:25.124 align:start size:84% position:16%
ERIN: What's going on
with this kitty,

00:05:25.124 --> 00:05:26.559 align:start size:78% position:22%
or can you give me
the backstory?

00:05:26.559 --> 00:05:29.895
MARY: Sure, Spot is one
of the neighborhood cats.

00:05:29.895 --> 00:05:33.432 align:start position:0%
We have house cats, and we have
what we call garage cats

00:05:33.432 --> 00:05:36.268
who will come by
for food, water,

00:05:36.268 --> 00:05:38.304
and a warm, dry place to sleep.

00:05:38.304 --> 00:05:40.739
I've seen him eat recently,

00:05:40.739 --> 00:05:44.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he licks very carefully
at wet food

00:05:44.276 --> 00:05:46.145 align:start size:81% position:19%
and he'll take
like a half a bite,

00:05:46.145 --> 00:05:48.447
but he never really
closes his mouth.

00:05:48.447 --> 00:05:49.882
BEN: It's possible
he likes canned food

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:51.250
because his mouth hurts.

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:54.587
ERIN: Scale of one to ten,
you know, one being like,

00:05:54.587 --> 00:05:55.955 align:start size:88% position:13%
you could sleep with him
in your bed

00:05:55.955 --> 00:05:57.390 align:start size:81% position:19%
and ten being like,
he would run.

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:59.591 align:start size:97% position:3%
MARY: I think we're
at about a seven or an eight.

00:05:59.591 --> 00:06:00.593
ERIN: Okay.

00:06:00.593 --> 00:06:01.693 align:start size:88% position:13%
BEN: Oh, he's
pretty feral, then. Wow.

00:06:01.693 --> 00:06:03.395
MARY: I have never
touched this cat.

00:06:03.395 --> 00:06:05.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
ERIN: Because this cat lives
on the streets

00:06:05.564 --> 00:06:07.200
without no particular owner,

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:09.535 align:start size:88% position:13%
we have to assume
that it's unvaccinated.

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:11.570 align:start position:0%
BEN: Let's get some long sleeves
on this guy.

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:12.705
And I'm gonna get my gloves.

00:06:12.705 --> 00:06:13.706 align:start size:84% position:16%
ERIN: Okay, Mary,
you got long sleeves?

00:06:13.706 --> 00:06:15.073
MARY: I will go get some.

00:06:15.073 --> 00:06:17.176 align:start position:0%
ERIN: It's a great idea
to wear long sleeves and gloves

00:06:17.176 --> 00:06:18.377
to protect ourselves,

00:06:18.377 --> 00:06:20.679 align:start size:91% position:9%
just in case this kitty's
claws come out.

00:06:20.679 --> 00:06:22.714
If they scratch you or bite you,

00:06:22.714 --> 00:06:25.684 align:start size:97% position:3%
kitties can transmit bacteria
through those wounds.

00:06:25.684 --> 00:06:27.820
These are like,
very tiny gloves.

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:28.821
I can't get my hands.

00:06:28.821 --> 00:06:30.689
CHASE: You want me
to get them off?

00:06:30.689 --> 00:06:32.224 align:start size:88% position:13%
ERIN: I got giant hands.
Man hands.

00:06:32.224 --> 00:06:33.325
CHASE: Five-year-olds, Mom.

00:06:33.325 --> 00:06:34.326
I can't even get
my hand in there.

00:06:34.326 --> 00:06:35.361
ERIN: I think they're Mary's.

00:06:35.361 --> 00:06:37.730 align:start size:88% position:13%
She has like,
normal lady-sized hands.

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:39.232
Oh, I see his face.

00:06:39.232 --> 00:06:41.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
BEN: He's right down there?
Oh, yeah!

00:06:41.534 --> 00:06:43.603
MARY: He could come zipping
out of there at any moment.

00:06:43.603 --> 00:06:44.937
ERIN: What if we put
the carrier there?

00:06:44.937 --> 00:06:45.938
MARY: In front?

00:06:45.938 --> 00:06:47.606 align:start size:78% position:22%
CHASE: We can just
grab his torso.

00:06:47.606 --> 00:06:49.041
ERIN: No, he's not, he's wild.

00:06:49.041 --> 00:06:50.108
We can't just pick him up.

00:06:50.108 --> 00:06:51.110
BEN: He's never been touched.

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:52.444
I like your plan, guys.

00:06:52.444 --> 00:06:54.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
Open up the front
of the carrier to this side.

00:06:54.413 --> 00:06:55.748
ERIN: Yep.

00:06:55.748 --> 00:06:57.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
BEN: Maybe we'll stick
a broom down the other side

00:06:57.216 --> 00:06:58.751 align:start size:91% position:9%
and just kind of scoot him
from the back

00:06:58.751 --> 00:07:00.119
and see if he goes forward.

00:07:00.119 --> 00:07:02.754 align:start size:91% position:9%
'Cause I wanna stick this
along the backside.

00:07:02.754 --> 00:07:04.123 align:start size:88% position:13%
ERIN: Honey, that might
spook him.

00:07:04.123 --> 00:07:05.357 align:start size:91% position:9%
BEN: Well, I know,
but what am I going to do?

00:07:05.357 --> 00:07:07.092
That's the whole plan.

00:07:07.092 --> 00:07:08.193
ERIN: I think you should

00:07:08.193 --> 00:07:09.929
just sort of gently
lay something there.

00:07:09.929 --> 00:07:12.632 align:start size:88% position:13%
BEN: There's a lot
of ideas going on here.

00:07:12.632 --> 00:07:15.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay, let's get that carrier
right in that spot, Erin.

00:07:15.434 --> 00:07:16.435
Let's see what happens.

00:07:16.435 --> 00:07:18.003
CHASE: Push him.

00:07:18.003 --> 00:07:19.204 align:start size:91% position:9%
BEN: Did he go in?
ERIN: He's looking at me.

00:07:19.204 --> 00:07:20.272
BEN: Oh, he's looking.

00:07:20.272 --> 00:07:21.340 align:start size:88% position:13%
He doesn't want
to really go in. Go in.

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:22.341
ERIN: He's headed
out the other way.

00:07:22.341 --> 00:07:24.376
BEN: He's turned around.

00:07:24.376 --> 00:07:25.777
MARY: There we go.
BEN: He's moving.

00:07:25.777 --> 00:07:26.945
ERIN: He's backing up a little.

00:07:26.945 --> 00:07:28.280
BEN: He's backing up.
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh!

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:29.615
