to hold the two pieces
of body wall together,

00:16:40.299 --> 00:16:41.566
that's ground zero.

00:16:41.566 --> 00:16:43.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
Erin and I decided let's do
half of it first,

00:16:43.601 --> 00:16:45.937 align:start size:97% position:3%
and then we work from the back
up to the towel clamps

00:16:45.937 --> 00:16:48.473 align:start position:0%
so we met in the middle,
and if one of those would break,

00:16:48.473 --> 00:16:51.744 align:start size:88% position:13%
we still have half of it
that's holding.

00:16:51.744 --> 00:16:54.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay, so, we've got
the top half sewn together.

00:16:54.213 --> 00:16:56.115
Now we got to work
on the bottom half.

00:17:08.160 --> 00:17:10.028 line:0%
BEN: Okay.

00:17:10.028 --> 00:17:13.031
That was a good bite.

00:17:13.031 --> 00:17:15.300
One more, okay?

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:17.469 align:start size:91% position:9%
You at first have to close
the body wall,

00:17:17.469 --> 00:17:19.671 align:start size:88% position:13%
then you close
the subcutaneous layer,

00:17:19.671 --> 00:17:21.473
and then you close
the skin after that.

00:17:21.473 --> 00:17:24.342
A three-layer closure has
more strength and stability

00:17:24.342 --> 00:17:27.746
than if you were just to close
everything all in one big swoop.

00:17:27.746 --> 00:17:29.481
That looks pretty good.

00:17:29.481 --> 00:17:30.482
Thanks for your help.

00:17:30.482 --> 00:17:32.084
ERIN: You betcha, baby.

00:17:32.084 --> 00:17:33.518
BEN: I've just fixed
the biggest hernia

00:17:33.518 --> 00:17:35.587 align:start size:81% position:19%
I've ever fixed
in my whole career.

00:17:35.587 --> 00:17:37.823 align:start size:84% position:16%
But just because
this surgery went well

00:17:37.823 --> 00:17:39.725 align:start size:88% position:13%
doesn't mean this calf's
in the clear.

00:17:39.725 --> 00:17:42.393
Tomorrow she'll go home
and recover on the farm.

00:17:42.393 --> 00:17:44.396 align:start size:84% position:16%
Austin will have to
keep her clean and dry

00:17:44.396 --> 00:17:46.264 align:start size:91% position:9%
and make sure she doesn't
eat too much

00:17:46.264 --> 00:17:47.699
and stretch out that new belly.

00:17:47.699 --> 00:17:52.704
♪ ♪

00:17:52.704 --> 00:17:57.208
♪ ♪

00:17:57.208 --> 00:17:59.110 align:start size:78% position:22%
ERIN: Hey, honey.
BEN: Hi.

00:17:59.110 --> 00:18:01.713
ERIN: I need to talk
with you on something.

00:18:01.713 --> 00:18:05.450
You know what I'm really
kind of missing is a dog.

00:18:05.450 --> 00:18:06.785
BEN: A dog?

00:18:06.785 --> 00:18:09.321
ERIN: I was thinking maybe
it would be a good thing

00:18:09.321 --> 00:18:11.256
for the boys maybe
to have some chores.

00:18:11.256 --> 00:18:12.591
This might even be for us.

00:18:12.591 --> 00:18:14.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're going to be
out of the house soon, so...

00:18:14.359 --> 00:18:15.861 align:start size:88% position:13%
BEN: Yeah, we might need
a companion

00:18:15.861 --> 00:18:17.195
in a few years ourselves.

00:18:17.195 --> 00:18:18.330
ERIN: I'll have to
just talk to you.

00:18:18.330 --> 00:18:19.364
BEN: We don't want that.

00:18:19.364 --> 00:18:20.432
ERIN: You on board?

00:18:20.432 --> 00:18:21.500
BEN: I am.

00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:23.468
Erin is often asking
about new animals.

00:18:23.468 --> 00:18:25.870 align:start size:88% position:13%
We always are talking
about getting a new pet,

00:18:25.870 --> 00:18:28.707
but it's tough to do
because we work a lot,

00:18:28.707 --> 00:18:32.143 align:start position:0%
but I don't really think there's
any stopping her this time.

00:18:32.143 --> 00:18:33.145
What do you got in mind?

00:18:33.145 --> 00:18:34.880
ERIN: Well...

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:36.514
BEN: Oh, you've been
searching already.

00:18:36.514 --> 00:18:37.649
This is a real thing.

00:18:37.649 --> 00:18:39.284
ERIN: Yeah. You know me.

00:18:39.284 --> 00:18:41.386 align:start size:84% position:16%
I like to online shop,
but Chase and I

00:18:41.386 --> 00:18:44.823 align:start size:91% position:9%
kind of were looking,
and I found one named Bud.

00:18:44.823 --> 00:18:45.891
BEN: Bud looks nice.

00:18:45.891 --> 00:18:47.826 align:start size:88% position:13%
ERIN: He just came
available for adoption.

00:18:47.826 --> 00:18:49.428
This could be the one.

00:18:51.863 --> 00:18:58.803
♪ ♪

00:18:58.803 --> 00:19:00.305 align:start size:72% position:28%
Come on, Spot.
Mom's here.

00:19:00.305 --> 00:19:03.375
Spot has recovered wonderfully
after her surgery yesterday.

00:19:03.375 --> 00:19:04.375
Hi, Mary.

00:19:04.375 --> 00:19:05.910
MARY: Hello.

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:08.080
ERIN: She's eating well,
she's gone to the bathroom,

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:11.483 align:start size:91% position:9%
and she is ready to return
to the great outdoors.

00:19:11.483 --> 00:19:14.152
Your cat radar was on fire,

00:19:14.152 --> 00:19:17.289 line:0%
and she did have a tooth
with a resorptive lesion.

00:19:17.289 --> 00:19:19.457 line:0%
That very sensitive portion
